# The lamp housings, which emit as well as reflect — the emissive is why the fittings read as
# the source of the light rather than as objects lit by it.
#
# ⚠ The emissive is a luminance in cd/m², not a multiplier, because everything else in this level is
# photometric now: the sun is sixteen thousand lux and the tonemap is exposed at EV 14.2, so an
# emissive of 6 would come out black. Three thousand nits is about a frosted lantern globe — bright
# enough to read as a source, dim enough not to clip the whole fitting to white. The colour is the
# 1900 K filament the light beside it declares.
shader: ForwardPlus
shading: StandardShading
features:
  - !MetalRoughness
    baseColor: 0.16 0.15 0.14
    metalness: 0.6
    roughness: 0.40
  - !Emissive
    emissiveColor: 1.0 0.52 0.20
    intensity: 3000
